an an intimate desk still life; preserve clear focal hierarchy around the map and journal, with stretches of table wood, map margin, and blank paper for crop tolerance\nVisual Hierarchy: Primary: partially unfolded estate map or garden plan paired with one open journal · Secondary: folded correspondence, ledger or catalog book, and botanical plate · Tertiary: brass dividers, spectacles, ribbon-tied packet, paper weights, bound journals, margin annotations, and indexing marks\nSupporting Objects: brass dividers or compass; reading spectacles; ribbon-tied packet; paper weights; bound journals from different periods; margin annotations; indexing marks\n\n[MATERIALS AND LIGHTING]\nAged oak or walnut table; heavy cotton rag and laid papers with subtle deckled edges; leather and cloth bindings; brass tools; cotton or silk ribbon; graphite and iron-gall ink; faded map pigments\nLighting: natural library daylight or restrained warm non-electrical lamp light, with believable direction and no theatrical effects\n\n[TEXT POLICY]\nvisible names, dates, places, map labels, and annotations must be approved, intentionally legible, or omitted; no pseudo-text\n\n[CANON POLICY]\nsupport approved Wychcombe canon without fixing unapproved geography or introducing new institutions, events, ownership facts, or chronology\nCanon Dependency: Supports Canon\nCanon Record: Living Memory (Accepted)\n\n[3AE04EB4-BF02-81AD-A281-D353BD9A704E]\nPurpose\nProvides the stable visual DNA for Wychcombe across canon references, environments, characters, artifacts, and product artwork.\nPrompt Assembly Position\nPlace this module first, before subject and composition instructions.\nContinuity Rules\nAtmosphere is restrained, not melodramatic.\nHistorical detail must feel inhabited and specific.\nMystery is communicated through evidence, omission, and arrangement.\nAvoid visual spectacle that overwhelms narrative meaning.\nAge should appear through use, repair, fading, patina, and custody rather than indiscriminate damage.\n\n[3AE04EB4-BF02-81AF-A302-C9A5EF68876E]\nPurpose\nDefines the recurring visual system for curated evidence layouts associated with the Wychcombe Journal Collection.\nRequired Behaviors\nObjects must imply relationships.\nAt least one focal object should anchor the composition.\nSupporting items should reinforce a clue, person, place, or time period.\nSurfaces should show realistic handling and age.\nNegative space should remain available for readability and product use.\nRecommended Uses\nVolume mood boards\nEphemera collections\nArtifact presentation\nProduct covers and marketing crops\nCanon-reference still lifes\n\n[3AE04EB4-BF02-81B0-AD10-EAD1DADD761B]\nMaterial Standard\nMaterials should remain visually distinct. Paper should not resemble leather; tarnished brass should not resemble painted gold; faded ink should remain legible where the story requires it.\nAging Standard\nAge is evidence. Each mark should suggest use, storage, repair, ownership, or time rather than serve as indiscriminate decoration.\nProduct Application\nFor printable ephemera, maintain sufficient edge clarity and tonal separation for cutting, layering, and home printing.\n\n[3AE04EB4-BF02-8131-849E-CAA5C7E908F9]\nLighting Intent\nWychcombe lighting should feel observed rather than staged.\nPreferred Conditions\nOvercast daylight through old glass\nSide light across paper and wood grain\nLate-afternoon warmth kept muted\nSmall practical lamps within otherwise natural scenes\nSoft shadow transitions with readable detail\nContinuity Rule\nLighting may create uncertainty, but it must not conceal essential canonical features of a subject.\n\n[3AE04EB4-BF02-81A2-9123-C82C280737AC]\nPurpose\nProvides the mandatory exclusion layer for Wychcombe image generation.\nGovernance Rules\nDo not remove a constraint merely to improve visual drama.\nAdd temporary record-specific exclusions in the asset prompt.\nRevise this module only when a formal visual-style decision changes.\nDo not 