s are expressed as evidence and narrative context, not what the facts are, The asset distinguishes between established information and suggestion, leaving uncertainty intact where canon does not provide an answer, A restrained number of meaningful details rewards close observation without turning every object into a clue, It does not control rendering style, palette, material appearance, technical production requirements, component format, allow Atmospheric Grounding or visual styling modules to turn neutral objects into implied clues merely for mood, Conversely, when approved canon establishes meaningful evidence, visual modules should support its presentation without obscuring or sensationalizing it, visual elements and rendering treatments that break the illustrated Victorian archival system, glossy 3D materials, game-rendering aesthetics, polished digital illustration that reads as synthetic rather than tactile and archival, modern or anachronistic materials and objects including plastics, ballpoint pens, contemporary electrical devices, modern packaging, barcodes, QR codes, synthetic ribbon, modern office supplies, contemporary signage, digital screens, modern typography, other clearly post-period visual language unless explicitly required by the Production Spec, clean digital white, neon color, bright synthetic saturation, mirror-polished metal, hard digital gradients, artificial glow, fog effects, theatrical lighting, any treatment that turns quiet archival imagery into spectacle, use generic antique-shop clutter, luxury stationery styling, cottagecore spectacle, gothic fantasy, horror aesthetics, steampunk machinery, faux-vintage craft-store decoration, uniform distressing, arbitrary “old-fashioned” embellishment, generate pseudo-text, modern labels, unsupported logos, invented institutional marks, fake historical branding, decorative text that appears factual but lacks an approved source, The goal is not merely to appear old, modern objects, plastics, elect