ical. ## Targeting ### Applicable Component Types Hero Paper, Coordinating Paper, Journal Card, Ephemera, Pocket, Envelope, Tag, Label, Hidden Discovery, Packaging and Marketing assets. Use wherever the Volume I visual atmosphere should remain consistent across the collection. ### Canon Dependency Hint Supports Canon. ### Priority / Injection Order Inject early in shared_prompt, after World & Collection Context and before component-specific composition, object, botanical, typography, or production instructions. ## Quality & Interactions ### Good Output Indicators The image feels quiet, tactile, and accumulated through use rather than staged or commercially styled. Materials read distinctly and plausibly, such as aged paper, worn wood, weathered brass, glass, terracotta, linen, or pressed botanicals when present. Color remains muted and natural, with cream, botanical greens, walnut, charcoal, sepia, and restrained warm accents rather than bright or synthetic color. The overall atmosphere supports scholarly observation, botanical care, and gentle discovery while leaving sufficient visual quiet for the component's intended function. ### Bad Output Indicators (reject if present) Lighting becomes cinematic, theatrical, magical, excessively dark, high-contrast, or dominated by glow or fog effects. Colors become highly saturated, jewel-toned, synthetically green, heavily sepia, or otherwise inconsistent with the muted natural palette. The scene becomes generic antique-shop clutter, excessive vintage decoration, gothic fantasy, horror, cottagecore spectacle, or luxury stationery. Aging becomes uniform grunge or excessive distressing rather than plausible evidence of handling, use, and material age. ### Module Interactions Pair with World & Collection Context modules for Wychcombe and Volume I, component-specific composition modules, approved object or botanical modules, typography modules, and production/output modules. The governing Style Guide remains authoritative for visual language. World and canon modules remain authoritative for factual content. Production Specification requirements take precedence for the individual asset's dimensions, function, required content, and output constraints. If another module introduces conflicting atmosphere or visual treatment, resolve the conflict in favor of the governing Style Guide rather than blending incompatible styles.\nWychcombe is a Victorian estate given over to the quiet work of preservation — a place where botanical specimens are pressed and catalogued, where archives accumulate in climate-controlled stillness, and where scholarship proceeds at the pace of careful hands. The estate comprises a main house of honeyed stone, a sprawling greenhouse complex with ironwork gone soft with verdigris, outbuildings converted to workrooms and storage, and grounds that blur the line between curated garden and managed wilderness. Gravel paths, the creak of wooden drawers, the scratch of nib on paper. Time moves differently here: seasons matter more than hours, and the work of a single afternoon might continue research begun three generations prior. Visually, Wychcombe exists in a palette of **aged naturals** — ivory paper darkened to cream, green in every muted variation from moss to fern, the warm brown of walnut cases and sepia ink, brass worn to a soft glow. Color is restrained when it appears (a terracotta pot, a burgundy wax seal), it carries weight. This is a world of **things that endure** and the people who tend them — where meaning accumulates through proximity, repetition, and care.\n| Paper Fine fiber, subtle tooth, restrained foxing, use-based wear | Wood Visible grain, soft edge wear, matte finish | Brass Soft patina, warm highlights | Glass Clouding, age, condensation, slight waviness | Botanicals Realistic fibers, veins, flattening, and discoloration |\n\n[NEGATIVE AND WRITING SPACE]\nPreserve 20% usable visual space.\n\n[CANON CONSTRAINTS]\nCanon dependency: Supports Canon Canon co